---
/**
 * /chain/daily-mint: The Daily Mint, the PointCast devnet's play auction. One
 * lot a UTC day, bids in devnet play ATTN (no value, never promised, may
 * reset), the winner's card minted on chain. The page reads the house from the
 * visitor's browser (lazily, genesis pinned), draws the open lot and the last
 * seven, lets anyone replay every sealed block through the auction's own law to
 * check the house against the chain, and lets a visitor bid with a key made in
 * their browser: faucet, optional card words, a transfer to the auctioneer.
 * It writes only when the visitor presses a send button after reading, in
 * plain words, exactly what will be sent.
 *
 * The logic is public/chain/apps/daily-mint.js (no DOM, importable by node), the
 * DOM side daily-mint-view.js, the shared key panel key-panel.js, the words
 * src/data/chain-app-daily-mint.ts. The settle law is the chain's own
 * sdk/daily-law.js, copied unchanged to public/chain/first-mints/lib/. The
 * devnet pins come from src/data/chain-home.ts, never typed here.
 *
 * ?devnet=http://127.0.0.1:PORT points the page at a local devnet for
 * end-to-end runs (scripts/e2e-chain-app-daily-mint.mjs). It is honoured only
 * for the hosts localhost and 127.0.0.1.
 */
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import ChainHeader from '../../components/chain/ChainHeader.astro';
import KeyPanel from '../../components/chain/KeyPanel.astro';
import Snippet from '../../components/chain/Snippet.astro';
import { CHANNELS } from '../../lib/channels';
import { DEVNET, DEVNET_PREVIOUS, RESET, assertDevnetLaunchPinned, notYet } from '../../data/chain-home';
import { APP, BID_COPY, CANNOT_SEE, CHECK_COPY, DAY_STEPS, HONESTY_LINE, LAW_PATH, auditSnippet } from '../../data/chain-app-daily-mint';

assertDevnetLaunchPinned();
import '../../styles/chain.css';
import '../../styles/chain-apps.css';

const ch = CHANNELS.FD;
const D = DEVNET.url;
const quick = [
  { label: 'Observatory', href: '/chain/observatory' },
  { label: 'Verify a block', href: '/chain/verify-a-block' },
  { label: 'Block Yard', href: DEVNET.yardHref },
  { label: 'Bots guide', href: '/chain/bots' },
];
const title = APP.title + ': a play auction on the PointCast devnet';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: APP.title,
  description: APP.description,
  url: 'https://pointcast.xyz' + APP.path + '/',
  applicationCategory: 'GameApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any modern browser',
  datePublished: '2026-10-20',
  dateModified: '2026-10-20',
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'PointCast Chain', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/chain' },
};
const ramp = '--ca-l50:' + ch.color50 + ';--ca-l600:' + ch.color600 + ';--ca-l800:' + ch.color800;
---

<BlockLayout title={title} description={APP.description} jsonLd={jsonLd} hideAds>
  <div class="chn ca-page dm-page" style={ramp}>
    <ChainHeader current="daily-mint" trail={[{ label: 'daily mint' }]} block={APP.block} quick={quick} />

    <header class="hero">
      <p class="kicker">CHAIN · APP · THE DAILY MINT · PLAY AUCTION · PUBLIC DEVNET-2 · NO VALUE · MAY RESET, NEVER SILENTLY</p>
      <h1>One card a day, auctioned in play money.</h1>
      <p class="dek">
        Every UTC day the devnet opens one lot. Anyone with play ATTN can bid; the highest bid at the close wins that day’s
        card, minted on chain. Everything the house does, every bid, refund and mint, is a block anyone can read, so this page
        can replay the auction itself and tell you whether the house kept to its own rules.
      </p>
      <svg class="ca-art" viewBox="0 0 360 72" role="img" aria-label="Three concentric rings beside a small card outline and a rising bar">
        <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
          <circle cx="44" cy="36" r="10" />
          <circle cx="44" cy="36" r="20" />
          <circle cx="44" cy="36" r="30" />
          <rect x="120" y="10" width="48" height="52" />
          <path d="M132 24h24M132 34h16M132 44h20" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M210 62V50M236 62V42M262 62V32M288 62V20M314 62V10" stroke-width="6" />
        </g>
      </svg>
      <p class="ca-honest" role="note" id="honesty">
        <b>{HONESTY_LINE}.</b> The Daily Mint is a play auction: bids are devnet play ATTN, which has no value and is never
        promised any, and the devnet may reset and take every card with it. A reset is dated and recorded, never silent: devnet-1
        was reset on {notYet(RESET.date)} and its recording is still checkable at <a href={DEVNET_PREVIOUS.path}>{DEVNET_PREVIOUS.path}</a>.
        Nothing here is a sale and nothing leads to a real market. The house is also the sequencer: it can refuse a bid it sees,
        and a signature or a bid is an accountable claim by a key, not proof of who holds it.
      </p>
      <p class="jump"><a href="#lot">today’s lot</a><a href="#check">check the house</a><a href="#bid">bid</a><a href="#law">the law</a></p>
    </header>

    <section
      id="lot"
      class="sec"
      aria-labelledby="lot-title"
      data-daily-mint-app
      data-state="static"
      data-api={D}
      data-genesis={DEVNET.genesis}
      data-chain-id={DEVNET.chainId}
    >
      <p class="kicker">01 · TODAY’S LOT · READ LIVE FROM THE DEVNET, IN YOUR BROWSER</p>
      <h2 id="lot-title" class="h2">The lot on the block, and the last seven.</h2>
      <noscript><p class="fine">The page needs JavaScript, because it reads the devnet and draws each card in your browser. The same lot is at <a href={D + '/daily'}>GET /daily</a> as JSON.</p></noscript>
      <p class="ca-status" data-dm-status role="status" aria-live="polite">The page reads <code>GET /status</code> and <code>GET /daily</code> once this section is on screen, then every ten seconds while the tab is visible.</p>
      <p class="ca-meta" data-dm-meta></p>
      <p class="ca-banner" data-dm-genesis role="note" hidden></p>
      <p class="note dm-house" data-dm-house></p>

      <div class="dm-lot">
        <div class="dm-card" data-dm-card><p class="ca-empty">Waiting for the first read.</p></div>
        <div class="dm-lotinfo">
          <p class="card__k">THE OPEN LOT</p>
          <p class="dm-lotn" data-dm-lot-n>–</p>
          <p class="fine" data-dm-lot-day></p>
          <div class="ca-tiles dm-tiles">
            <div class="ca-tile ca-tile--hero" data-dm-closes-bar><span class="ca-tile__k">Closes in</span><span class="ca-tile__v" data-dm-closes>–</span></div>
            <div class="ca-tile"><span class="ca-tile__k">Least bid</span><span class="ca-tile__v" data-dm-minbid>–</span></div>
            <div class="ca-tile"><span class="ca-tile__k">Bids</span><span class="ca-tile__v" data-dm-bids>–</span></div>
            <div class="ca-tile"><span class="ca-tile__k">Leading</span><span class="ca-tile__v dm-leader" data-dm-leader>–</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="fine" data-dm-card-note></p>
          <p class="fine" data-dm-tally></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="h3">The last seven lots</h3>
      <div class="tbl">
        <table>
          <caption>The most recent lots, newest first, with their cards drawn from the recipes on chain</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Lot</th><th scope="col">Day (UTC)</th><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Bids</th><th scope="col">Minted to</th><th scope="col">Card</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody data-dm-recent><tr><td colspan="6">Waiting for the first read.</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="h3">How a lot goes</h3>
      <ol class="ca-steps dm-steps">
        {DAY_STEPS.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="ca-step">
            <div class="ca-step__h"><span class="ca-step__n" aria-hidden="true">{i + 1}</span><h4 class="ca-step__t">{s.title}</h4></div>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <h3 class="h3">The house, by the numbers</h3>
      <dl class="ca-kv" data-dm-rules></dl>
      <dl class="ca-kv">
        <div><dt>Auctioneer</dt><dd><code class="ca-hash" data-dm-auctioneer>–</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Faucet</dt><dd><code class="ca-hash" data-dm-faucet-addr>–</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Town Shelf</dt><dd><code class="ca-hash" data-dm-shelf>–</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Newest block</dt><dd data-dm-height>–</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <section id="check" class="dm-sec" aria-labelledby="check-title">
        <p class="kicker">02 · CHECK THE HOUSE · YOUR BROWSER REPLAYS THE AUCTION</p>
        <h2 id="check-title" class="h2">Did the house keep to its own rules?</h2>
        <p class="note">{CHECK_COPY.what}</p>
        <p class="ca-actions">
          <button class="btn" type="button" data-dm-audit disabled>{CHECK_COPY.button}</button>
          <span class="fine">Reads every sealed block in pages of 500 (GET only), then does the sums here. Nothing is written.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="ca-result dm-audit" data-dm-audit-summary role="status" aria-live="polite" data-state="idle">Not run yet.</p>
        <ul class="ca-checks" data-dm-audit-out aria-label="One line per lot"></ul>
        <h3 class="h3">What the check cannot see</h3>
        <ul class="bullets">{CANNOT_SEE.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>

      <section id="bid" class="dm-sec" aria-labelledby="bid-title">
        <p class="kicker">03 · BID · A KEY MADE IN YOUR BROWSER · NOTHING IS SENT UNTIL YOU PRESS SEND</p>
        <h2 id="bid-title" class="h2">Take the faucet’s 100, bid, win a card.</h2>
        <p class="note">
          Three steps: make a key, take the faucet’s 100 play ATTN once, then bid. Before anything is sent the page lists, in plain
          words, exactly what will go to the devnet. {BID_COPY.warn}
        </p>
        <KeyPanel signs="the bid and the card words" id="dm-kp" />
        <p class="ca-meta">Play ATTN held by this key: <b data-dm-balance>make a key first</b></p>
        <p class="ca-meta" data-dm-mybid role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="ca-actions">
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-dm-faucet disabled>Ask the faucet for 100 play ATTN</button>
          <span class="fine" data-dm-faucet-out>Once per address; three an address and 300 in all each UTC day.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="ca-controls">
          <div class="ca-field">
            <label class="ca-label" for="dm-amount">Your bid, in play ATTN</label>
            <input id="dm-amount" class="ca-input ca-input--mono ca-input--fit dm-amount" data-dm-amount type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="12" disabled />
          </div>
          <div class="ca-field ca-field--grow">
            <label class="ca-label" for="dm-gift">Give the card to (optional)</label>
            <input id="dm-gift" class="ca-input ca-input--mono" data-dm-gift type="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="64" placeholder="a tz1, tz2 or pcp1 address" disabled />
          </div>
        </div>
        <fieldset class="dm-words">
          <legend>Up to three words for the card (optional)</legend>
          <div class="dm-words__grid" data-dm-words></div>
        </fieldset>
        <p class="ca-actions"><button class="btn" type="button" data-dm-review disabled>Review the bid</button></p>
        <ul class="ca-confirm dm-errors" data-dm-errors role="alert" hidden></ul>
        <div class="ca-confirm" data-dm-confirm hidden>
          <p><b>You are about to send, to the public devnet:</b></p>
          <ul data-dm-confirm-list></ul>
          <p data-dm-confirm-where></p>
          <p>{BID_COPY.warn}</p>
          <p class="ca-actions">
            <button class="btn" type="button" data-dm-send>Send the bid</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-dm-cancel>Cancel</button>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ca-result" data-dm-result hidden role="status" aria-live="polite"><h3>Result</h3><p data-dm-result-text></p></div>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section id="law" class="sec" aria-labelledby="law-title">
      <p class="kicker">04 · THE LAW, IN CODE</p>
      <h2 id="law-title" class="h2">The same check from a terminal.</h2>
      <p class="note">
        The auction’s rules are one pure function of the blocks, <a href={LAW_PATH}>daily-law.js</a>: the house runs it to decide what
        it owes, and this page and a script run it to check. The code is the chain’s own, copied unchanged.
      </p>
      <Snippet label="audit-daily.mjs · from a copy of pointcast-chain" code={auditSnippet(D)} />
    </section>

    <footer class="method">
      <p class="kicker">METHOD</p>
      <p>
        The lot and the history are what {D.replace('https://', '')} sends at GET /daily, checked against the genesis this page was
        built with. Each card is drawn in your browser from the recipe on chain with the First Mint renderer and audited before it
        is shown. The check replays every block through daily-law.js and compares with GET /daily/law. {HONESTY_LINE}; a reset is
        dated and recorded. Filed by Claude Code.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</BlockLayout>

<script is:inline type="module">
  // Lazy: nothing is imported or read until the page has loaded, the browser is idle, the lot is near the viewport and the tab is visible.
  const root = document.querySelector('[data-daily-mint-app]');
  if (root) {
    const idle = (fn) => (typeof requestIdleCallback === 'function' ? requestIdleCallback(fn, { timeout: 4000 }) : setTimeout(fn, 1200));
    const go = () => idle(() => import('/chain/apps/daily-mint-view.js').then((m) => m.start(root)).catch(() => { root.dataset.state = 'down'; }));
    if (document.readyState === 'complete') go(); else window.addEventListener('load', go, { once: true });
  }
</script>

<style is:global>
  .chn .dm-house{margin:10px 0 0}
  .chn .dm-lot{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,300px) minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px;align-items:start;margin:18px 0 0}
  .chn .dm-card{min-width:0;border:1.5px solid var(--c600);background:var(--c50);padding:10px;aspect-ratio:3 / 4;display:grid;place-items:center}
  .chn .dm-card__img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:100%}
  .chn .dm-lotn{margin:0;font:500 clamp(28px,4vw,40px)/1.1 var(--pc-font-sans);letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--pc-ink)}
  .chn .dm-tiles{margin-top:14px}
  .chn .dm-tiles .ca-tile--hero .ca-tile__v{font-size:clamp(26px,3.6vw,34px)}
  .chn .dm-leader{font-size:16px;line-height:1.4}
  .chn [data-dm-closes-bar][data-low="yes"] .ca-tile__v{color:var(--ca-warn)}
  .chn .dm-thumb{width:64px}
  .chn .dm-thumb__img{display:block;width:48px;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--pc-rule-soft)}
  .chn .dm-lot th.dm-lot{font:500 13px var(--pc-font-mono)}
  .chn .dm-steps{margin-top:8px}
  .chn .dm-steps h4{margin:0}
  .chn .dm-sec{padding-top:48px;scroll-margin-top:12px}
  .chn .dm-audit{margin-top:6px;border-color:var(--c600);border-left-width:6px}
  .chn .dm-audit[data-state="ok"]{border-color:var(--ca-ok)}
  .chn .dm-audit[data-state="bad"]{border-color:var(--ca-bad)}
  .chn .dm-audit[data-state="idle"],.chn .dm-audit[data-state="busy"]{border-color:var(--c600)}
  .chn .dm-amount{width:168px}
  .chn .dm-words{margin:14px 0 0;padding:12px 14px;border:1.5px solid var(--c600);border-radius:0;min-width:0}
  .chn .dm-words legend{padding:0 6px;font:500 10px/1.5 var(--pc-font-mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--c800)}
  .chn .dm-words__grid{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 14px}
  .chn .dm-word{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:36px;font:500 12px var(--pc-font-mono);letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--pc-ink);cursor:pointer}
  .chn .dm-errors{border-color:var(--ca-bad);border-style:solid}
  .chn .dm-errors[hidden]{display:none}
  @media (max-width:760px){
    .chn .dm-lot{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}
    .chn .dm-card{max-width:320px}
    .chn .dm-amount{width:100%}
  }
</style>
